<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">As-Salih Ismail</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1251</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as As-Salih Ismail, Emir of Damascus, al-Salih Ismail of Damascus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">As-Salih Ismail was an Ayyubid prince, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a> I, who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalbek">Baalbek</a> and ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> briefly in 1237 and again from 1239 to 1245. In his rivalry with his nephew as-Salih Ayyub, sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, he allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a> and ceded castles such as Beaufort to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, an act that scandalised Muslim opinion. He lost Damascus in 1245 and died in 1251.</p></div>
